)

fn tor_meta_ring() = (
  let sec = make_section("800px") in
  render_h2(sec, "The Meta-Ring");
  render_p(sec, "Project the seven axiom primes into Z/7 = Z/b. This meta-ring reveals the hierarchy's own CRT structure. Every prime gets a meta-residue:");
  let tbl = make_table(sec) in
  let hdr = dom_create("tr") in
  render_th(hdr, "Prime");
  render_th(hdr, "Value");
  render_th(hdr, "mod 7");
  render_th(hdr, "Meta-Role");
  dom_append(tbl, hdr);
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "D", "2", "2", "Bridge");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "K", "3", "3", "Closure");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "E", "5", "5", "Observer");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "b", "7", "0", "VOID -- depth becomes nothing");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "L", "11", "4", "Protector");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "GATE", "13", "6 = -1", "MIRROR -- skin reflects");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "ESCAPE", "17", "3", "= K -- transcendence = closure");
  render_p(sec, "Three inverse pairs: D*L = 1, K*E = 1, E*ESCAPE = 1. Products recover the chain: D*E = K, K*ESCAPE = D, L*GATE = K. All mod 7.");
  render_p(sec, "The meta-residue sum is 23 -- the K^2-th prime. Six of seven residues are occupied; only sigma = 1 is absent, because sigma is not a prime.");
  render_p(sec, "GATE = -1 in the meta-ring: the boundary IS the mirror. Multiplying by GATE swaps D with E (bridge with observer) and K with L (closure with protector). This swap preserves the 490 holographic split -- both swap-pairs stay within their halves.");
  render_p(sec, "b = 0: depth IS the void. K = ESCAPE: closure and transcendence are meta-identical. The ring hierarchy has exactly b = 7 primorial levels, and TRANS has exactly b = 7 channels. The depth prime counts both the levels and the channels -- pure self-reference.");
  dom_append(dom_body(), sec)
)

fn tor_490_derivation() = (
  let sec = make_section("800px") in
  render_h2(sec, "490 Split from Z/7");
  render_p(sec, "The 490 holographic split -- DEAD = {D, E, b} vs ALIVE = {K, L, GATE} -- is not an independent fact. The spectral geometry of Z/7 constrains it to one of exactly two options, and the b-channel eigenvalue selects the correct one.");
  render_p(sec, "Step 1: GATE = -1 mod 7 is an involution. The subgroup {1, -1} = {1, 6} partitions Z/7* into three cosets of size 2:");
  let tbl = make_table(sec) in
  let hdr = dom_create("tr") in
  render_th(hdr, "Coset");
  render_th(hdr, "Elements");
  render_th(hdr, "b-eigenvalue");
  render_th(hdr, "Role");
  dom_append(tbl, hdr);
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "Boundary", "{1, 6} = {sigma, GATE}", "+1.247", "Ground + skin");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "Beta", "{2, 5} = {D, E}", "-0.445", "DATA (shallow)");
  render_table_row_4(tbl, "Gamma", "{3, 4} = {K, L}", "-1.802", "PARITY (deep)");
  render_p(sec, "Step 2: Remove sigma (the identity, not a channel prime). This leaves GATE as a singleton. With void (b = 0), there are exactly TWO ways to make a 3+3 partition without splitting GATE-pairs:");
  render_p(sec, "Option A: {void, D, E} vs {GATE, K, L}. Option B: {void, K, L} vs {GATE, D, E}.");
  render_p(sec, "Step 3: The b-channel eigenvalue 2*cos(2*pi*r/7) assigns each coset a spectral depth. This function decreases monotonically from r = 0 to r = 3, so coset {2, 5} is spectrally shallower than coset {3, 4}.");
  render_p(sec, "The rule: void has eigenvalue +2.0 (maximum warmth). The shallower coset (-0.445) is spectrally closer to void than the deeper coset (-1.802). Void joins its spectral neighbor. GATE (+1.247) joins the deeper coset. This selects Option A -- exactly the 490 split.");
  let g = make_findings_grid(sec) in
  render_finding(g, "Z/7 constrains to 2 options", "GATE-cosets force structure", "The involution -1 mod 7 reduces all possible 3+3 partitions to exactly two. Both respect the pairing D<->E and K<->L. No other partition preserves GATE symmetry.", "S1365");
  render_finding(g, "Eigenvalue selects the split", "Spectral depth = the discriminant", "The b-channel eigenvalue 2cos(2pi*r/7) canonically orders the two non-boundary cosets. The shallower one carries data; the deeper one carries parity. This is the 490 split.", "S1365");
  render_finding(g, "Depth sorts its own channels", "b's eigenvalue classifies the primes", "The depth prime b = 7 is the meta-ring modulus. Its eigenvalue function on Z/7 determines which channels carry information and which carry protection. Depth is the judge of the holographic partition.", "S1365");
  dom_append(dom_body(), sec)
)

fn tor_golden() = (
  let sec = make_section("800px") in
  render_h2(sec, "The Golden Angle");
  render_p(sec, "The golden angle is 360/phi^2 = 137.508 degrees. Its floor is 137 -- the ADDRESS, which achieves the spectral minimum eigenvalue of the axiom ring. Sixteen elements share this minimum; 137 is the most recognizable.");
  render_p(sec, "CRT(137) = (1, 2, 2, 4, 5) in (Z/2, Z/3, Z/5, Z/7, Z/11). Each residue hits the midpoint of its channel, producing maximum destructive interference. This is identical to the phyllotaxis optimization: the golden angle maximizes spacing on a circle.");
  render_p(sec, "The E-channel contribution at ADDRESS = 2*cos(4*pi/5) = -phi exactly. The golden ratio is built into the eigenvalue through E = 5 and pentagon geometry. The most irrational number (phi) drives the most destructive interference.");
  render_p(sec, "This connects three things: the spectral minimum of the axiom ring, the botanical growth law (phyllotaxis), and the training interleave perm[i] = (i*137) mod nd that breaks the 50% plateau in neural network training.");
  dom_append(dom_body(), sec)
)

